 $oldtopic='3.4 Grouping and summary statistics';$topic='3.4 Grouping and summary statistics';
 $summary='<p>Aggregate detail into decision-sized group tables while making grain, counts, denominators, centre, spread, proportions, and reconciliation explicit.</p>';
 $oldpage='Lesson 10: Grouping and summary statistics';$oldlti='Python Lab 10: Grouping and statistics';$oldquiz='Knowledge check: Lesson 10: Grouping and summary statistics';
 $pagename='Lesson 3.4: Grouping and summary statistics';$ltiname='Python Lab 3.4: Grouping and summary statistics';$quizname='Knowledge check: 3.4 Grouping and summary statistics';
 $pageintro='<p>Define result grain and verify counts, statistics, rate denominators, and reconciliation.</p>';$quizintro='<p>Use short tables and code to check grain, groupby, counts, statistics, denominators, multiple keys, proportions, and reconciliation. Retry as needed; the highest score is kept.</p>';
 $body='<div class="python-sample-lesson"><h2>Define what one result row means before aggregation</h2><p>Lesson 3.3 produced analysis-ready detail. Aggregation now compresses those rows into a report. One detail row means centre-month-course; one district summary row means a district; one district-course row means that pair. Define this grain first or even a correct number may be impossible to explain.</p>'
 .'<h3>groupby splits, applies, and combines</h3><p><code>groupby("district")</code> splits matching rows, applies the same named aggregations, and combines results. Named <code>agg()</code> records output meaning; <code>reset_index()</code> restores group keys as ordinary columns.</p>'.v25_code("district = analysis.groupby(\"district\", dropna=False).agg(\n centre_months=(\"centre_id\",\"size\"), centres=(\"centre_id\",\"nunique\"), registered_total=(\"registered\",\"sum\")\n).reset_index()")
 .'<h3>Distinguish size, count, and nunique</h3><p><code>size</code> counts rows including missing values, <code>count</code> counts non-missing values in a selected column, and <code>nunique</code> counts distinct values. Centre-month records, reported attendance values, and distinct centres are different measures.</p>'
 .'<h3>Totals, centre, and spread answer different questions</h3><p><code>sum</code> measures volume, <code>mean</code> arithmetic centre, <code>median</code> the middle ordered value, <code>min</code> and <code>max</code> endpoints, and <code>std</code> spread around the mean. Extremes can pull the mean, so show count, median, and range. Standard deviation does not explain causes.</p>'.v25_code("analysis.groupby(\"course\")[\"registered\"].agg([\"size\",\"sum\",\"mean\",\"median\",\"min\",\"max\",\"std\"])")
 .'<h3>Aggregate compatible numerators and denominators before a rate</h3><p>Overall course completion is total completed divided by total registered. A simple mean of centre-month rates gives a small and a large record equal weight. It answers about a typical record, not all registered learners. State the denominator in words.</p>'.v25_code("course = analysis.groupby(\"course\").agg(records=(\"centre_id\",\"size\"),registered=(\"registered\",\"sum\"),completed=(\"completed\",\"sum\"),mean_row_rate=(\"completion_rate\",\"mean\"),material_cost=(\"material_cost\",\"sum\"))\ncourse[\"overall_completion_rate\"] = course[\"completed\"] / course[\"registered\"] * 100\ncourse[\"cost_per_completion\"] = course[\"material_cost\"] / course[\"completed\"]")
 .'<p>For Python Foundations in the practice data, the simple mean row rate is about 71.9%, while 290 total completions divided by 400 total registrations is 72.5%. Similar values still have different definitions.</p>'
 .'<h3>Multiple keys preserve hierarchy</h3><p><code>groupby(["district","course"])</code> creates one row per pair. This differs from district-only grain. Do not add or average incompatible grains without defining their relationship.</p>'
 .'<h3>State the proportion denominator and check 100%</h3><p>Course share within a district divides district-course registrations by that district total. The grand total answers another question. <code>transform("sum")</code> aligns denominators, and within-district shares should sum to 100%.</p>'.v25_code("dc[\"district_total\"] = dc.groupby(\"district\")[\"registered\"].transform(\"sum\")\ndc[\"share\"] = dc[\"registered\"] / dc[\"district_total\"] * 100")
 .'<h3>Reconcile grouped totals with detail</h3><p>Grouped record, registered, completed, and material-cost totals must sum back to analysis detail. Assertions expose omitted or double-counted data. Attach counts to averages and do not interpret a small-group difference as proof of cause or superiority.</p>'.v25_code("assert int(course[\"records\"].sum()) == len(analysis)\nassert course[\"registered\"].sum() == analysis[\"registered\"].sum()\nassert course[\"completed\"].sum() == analysis[\"completed\"].sum()")
 .'<h3>From worked example to transfer</h3><p>By month and course, calculate record count, distinct centres, registered, attended and completed totals, overall completion rate, material cost, and cost per completion. State denominators, compare with mean row rate, reconcile grand totals, and identify a small-count comparison.</p>'
 .'<p>You have reached the lesson goal when you can define grain, select count and summary functions, aggregate rate components, group by multiple keys, calculate proportions, and reconcile the result.</p><p><strong>Estimated study time:</strong> about 3 hours</p><p style="display:none">PYAI-V25-LESSON34-FLOW</p></div>';
 $questions=[
 v25_q('L34R-01','<p>Source grain is centre-month-course. After <code>groupby(["district","course"])</code>, what does one row mean?</p>',[['One district-course pair','Correct.'],['One centre only','Centre is not a key.'],['One month only','Month is not a key.'],['Always one source row','Rows are aggregated.']],0,'A unique key combination defines result grain.'),
 v25_q('L34R-02','<p>Ten rows contain one missing attendance. Which result is correct?</p>',[['attendance count=10, size=9','Reversed.'],['size=10, attendance count=9','Correct.'],['nunique must be 10','It counts distinct values.'],['sum must be 10','It sums values.']],1,'size counts rows; count excludes missing values in its column.'),
 v25_q('L34R-03','<p>For <code>[20,22,24,100]</code>, which centre is less affected by 100 than the mean?</p>',[['Sum','Not a centre.'],['Median','Correct: it is 23.'],['Maximum','An endpoint.'],['Standard deviation','Spread.']],1,'Median is based on ordered position.'),
 v25_q('L34R-04','<p>What does a large standard deviation directly indicate?</p>',[['Values are widely spread around the mean','Correct.'],['The cause of a group difference','It does not establish cause.'],['The mean is wrong','Not necessarily.'],['All values are missing','No.']],0,'Standard deviation measures spread, not cause.'),
 v25_q('L34R-05','<p>Rows are 10 registered/10 completed and 90/45. What is completion among all registered learners?</p>',[['75%, the mean of 100% and 50%','Equal row weighting.'],['55%, (10+45)/(10+90)','Correct.'],['50%, using only the large row','Both rows count.'],['45%, completed total alone','Missing denominator.']],1,'Aggregate compatible numerator and denominator.'),
 v25_q('L34R-06','<p>Why can mean row rate differ from ratio of totals?</p>',[['Rows have different denominators but the mean weights rows equally','Correct.'],['pandas uses randomness','No.'],['Median equals total','No.'],['groupby changes numbers to text','No.']],0,'The two statistics answer different questions.'),
 v25_q('L34R-07','<p>What denominator gives course registration share within a district?</p>',[['Grand total registration','That is share of all data.'],['Registration total for that district','Correct.'],['Number of course names','Wrong unit.'],['Row count only','Wrong denominator.']],1,'Within-district defines denominator scope.'),
 v25_q('L34R-08','<p>What matters when comparing district-course and district-only summaries?</p>',[['They have different grains and cannot be combined blindly','Correct.'],['They always have equal rows','No.'],['Delete district first','Loses hierarchy.'],['Convert course to a number','Unnecessary.']],0,'Define relationships between grains before combining.'),
 v25_q('L34R-09','<p>What directly validates within-district course shares?</p>',[['Shares sum to about 100% in each district','Correct.'],['All means equal 50','No.'],['Maximum equals registration total','Different units.'],['Standard deviation is zero','Not required.']],0,'Parts sharing one denominator sum to the whole.'),
 v25_q('L34R-10','<p>How do you check no registrations were lost in grouping?</p>',[['Compare sum of group registration totals with detail registration total','Correct.'],['Change chart colour','No check.'],['Delete the smallest group','Not reconciliation.'],['Display only means','Does not check volume.']],0,'Reconcile partial totals with source analysis detail.')];
